## Summary

The `SpaceCard` component currently defines its own `SpaceCardProps` interface with manually mapped properties (code, modificationDate, modifiedBy, etc.). This should be refactored to accept the `OpenbisSpace` entity type from `@/lib/model/OpenBISModel`, which provides the authoritative schema for Space entities. This ensures consistency, improves type safety, and prevents prop duplication.

## Source Location

**File:** [`components/dashboard/SpaceCard.server.tsx`](https://github.com/cckssr/NextLaBIS/blob/develop/nextapp/src/components/dashboard/SpaceCard.server.tsx#L24)
**Line:** 24

## Current Code Context

```typescript
/**
 * Props for SpaceCard component.
 * TODO: Replace with Space model type
 */
interface SpaceCardProps {
  code: string;
  modificationDate: Date;
  modifiedBy: string;
  numberOfProjects?: number;
  numberOfCollections?: number;
  description?: string;
  tags?: string[]; // TODO: Replace with proper Tag type
  spaceRights?: OpenBISRole; // TODO: Define proper type for roles / rights
}
```

**Available Entity Type:**

```typescript
// From src/lib/model/OpenBISModel.ts
export interface OpenbisSpace extends OpenbisEntityBase {
  kind: "SPACE";
  frozenForProjects?: boolean;
  frozenForObjects?: boolean;
}

export interface OpenbisEntityBase {
  kind: OpenbisEntityKind;
  permId: OpenbisPermId;
  code: string;
  registrationDate: Date;
  modificationDate: Date;
  registratedBy: OpenbisUser;
  frozen?: boolean;
  description?: string | null;
}
```

## Analysis

**Current Problem:**
- `SpaceCardProps` manually duplicates properties from the `OpenbisSpace` entity (code, modificationDate, description)
- Properties like `numberOfProjects`, `numberOfCollections`, and `spaceRights` are not part of the core Space model and mix domain data with display-specific concerns
- This manual mapping creates a maintenance burden: if `OpenbisSpace` changes, both the entity type and component props must be updated separately
- No single source of truth for what makes up a Space entity
- The `tags`, `spaceRights` fields are marked with TODOs, indicating they need proper typing

**Why This Matters:**
- **Type Safety**: Using the authoritative `OpenbisSpace` type ensures the component can only receive valid Space data
- **Scalability**: When Phase 1 adds API integration, data will come directly as `OpenbisSpace` objects; refactoring now prevents rework later
- **Consistency**: Other entity components (ProjectsTable, ObjectCard, etc.) should follow the same pattern
- **Code Quality**: Reduces duplication and props interface maintenance

**Related Code:**
- `src/lib/model/OpenBISModel.ts` - Contains `OpenbisSpace`, `OpenbisEntityBase`
- `src/types/openbis.ts` - Contains view model types like `SpaceDisplayData`
- `src/lib/spaces/model.ts` - Space-specific view models and transformations
- Parent component: `SpacesOverviewCard` passes individual Space properties

## Suggested Implementation

1. **Refactor component to accept `OpenbisSpace` + optional display props:**
   ```typescript
   interface SpaceCardProps {
     space: OpenbisSpace;
     numberOfProjects?: number;  // Display-specific, computed separately
     numberOfCollections?: number; // Display-specific, computed separately
     spaceRights?: OpenBISRole;  // Computed from user context, not from Space
     tags?: string[];  // Future: move to OpenbisSpace.tags
   }
   ```

2. **Update component to destructure from `space` object:**
   ```typescript
   export function SpaceCard({ space, numberOfProjects, numberOfCollections, ... }: SpaceCardProps) {
     const { code, modificationDate, description, registratedBy } = space;
     // Use registratedBy instead of "modifiedBy" (consistent with entity model)
   }
   ```

3. **Update parent component (`SpacesOverviewCard`) to pass full Space object:**
   ```typescript
   {spaces.slice(0, maxSpaceCount).map((space) => (
     <SpaceCard key={space.code} space={space} numberOfProjects={0} />
   ))}
   ```

4. **Extract computed display properties into data transformation layer:**
   - Move `numberOfProjects`, `numberOfCollections`, `spaceRights` calculation to a separate function in `lib/spaces/`
   - Return enriched view model: `SpaceCardDisplayData = OpenbisSpace & { numberOfProjects?: number; ... }`

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] `SpaceCardProps` accepts `space: OpenbisSpace` as primary prop
- [ ] Component destructures code, modificationDate, description from the space object
- [ ] TypeScript strict mode passes without errors
- [ ] `SpacesOverviewCard` updated to pass full Space object instead of individual props
- [ ] ESLint and build checks pass
- [ ] No breaking changes to other components using SpaceCard
- [ ] TODO comment updated with issue number

## Phase Alignment

**Phase 0 → Phase 1 Bridge** - This refactoring prepares the component architecture for Phase 1 API integration. Currently achievable with mock data; becomes critical when switching to real OpenBIS API responses.

## Priority

Medium - Improves code quality and prevents Phase 1 rework

